1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:05,730
In Argentina, almost one in three new cars sold comes from the same company.

2
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:06,846
In Brazil, too.

3
00:00:06,926 --> 00:00:09,848
That company is called Stellantis.

4
00:00:09,848 --> 00:00:15,520
Fiat, Peugeot, Citroën, Jeep, Ram… fourteen brands under one roof.

5
00:00:15,694 --> 00:00:19,374
And in 2025 it lost more than €22 billion.

6
00:00:19,374 --> 00:00:23,230
The first annual loss in its entire history.

7
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:28,165
How does a company go from breaking records to losing all that in just two years?

8
00:00:28,165 --> 00:00:29,543
And the strangest part:

9
00:00:29,543 --> 00:00:34,578
while it was sinking across half the world, in South America it was still the queen.

10
00:00:35,228 --> 00:00:36,080
Chapter one:

11
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,997
the wedding of the century.

12
00:00:38,348 --> 00:00:39,518
January 2021.

13
00:00:39,518 --> 00:00:41,588
Two giant groups merge:

14
00:00:41,588 --> 00:00:49,058
France's PSA, the maker of Peugeot and Citroën, and Italian-American FCA, the maker

15
00:00:49,058 --> 00:00:51,488
of Fiat, Chrysler and Jeep.

16
00:00:51,568 --> 00:00:55,242
FCA itself came from another incredible story:

17
00:00:55,242 --> 00:00:59,874
Fiat had taken over Chrysler after its bankruptcy in 2009.

18
00:01:00,103 --> 00:01:01,989
The merger was fifty-fifty:

19
00:01:01,989 --> 00:01:04,226
neither one swallowed the other.

20
00:01:04,226 --> 00:01:05,484
At least on paper.

21
00:01:06,853 --> 00:01:11,167
Stellantis is born, one of the biggest carmakers in the world.

22
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:15,760
Fourteen brands, from Fiat and Peugeot to Maserati and Alfa Romeo.

23
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:17,606
The name comes from Latin:

24
00:01:17,606 --> 00:01:20,391
"stello", meaning to brighten with stars.

25
00:01:20,391 --> 00:01:24,874
The idea was that together, all those brands would shine brighter.

26
00:01:24,954 --> 00:01:30,598
In charge they put Carlos Tavares, a Portuguese executive known as a numbers wizard:

27
00:01:30,598 --> 00:01:35,168
he had already rescued Peugeot and Opel when they were losing money.

28
00:01:35,383 --> 00:01:40,849
In 2014, Peugeot was in such bad shape that the French state and China's Dongfeng

29
00:01:40,849 --> 00:01:42,132
had to buy into it.

30
00:01:42,132 --> 00:01:45,911
Tavares arrived that year and brought it back to profit.

31
00:01:45,991 --> 00:01:50,875
Then he bought Opel, which had lost money for almost twenty years under General

32
00:01:50,875 --> 00:01:51,307
Motors.

33
00:01:51,307 --> 00:01:53,409
A year later, Opel was profitable.

34
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:55,168
His recipe was simple:

35
00:01:55,168 --> 00:01:58,586
cut costs wherever possible and raise margins.

36
00:01:58,586 --> 00:02:01,187
And at first it worked wonderfully.

37
00:02:02,424 --> 00:02:03,385
Chapter two:

38
00:02:03,385 --> 00:02:04,827
the money machine.

39
00:02:06,067 --> 00:02:11,332
In 2023, Stellantis earns about €18.6 billion.

40
00:02:11,332 --> 00:02:12,363
A record.

41
00:02:13,052 --> 00:02:16,060
A big part of it came from the United States:

42
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,269
Ram trucks and Jeeps sold at ever-higher prices.

43
00:02:20,272 --> 00:02:24,192
And Jeep is a brand with more than eighty years of history:

44
00:02:24,192 --> 00:02:25,720
it was born as the U.S.

45
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:27,978
Army's off-roader in World War II.

46
00:02:28,877 --> 00:02:30,426
Shareholders were happy.

47
00:02:30,426 --> 00:02:35,590
But inside the company, and at the dealerships, something was starting to crack.

48
00:02:35,914 --> 00:02:41,043
Because when you raise prices that much and cut that much on the inside, sooner or

49
00:02:41,043 --> 00:02:42,732
later someone stops buying.

50
00:02:43,395 --> 00:02:44,667
Chapter three:

51
00:02:44,667 --> 00:02:45,667
the cracks.

52
00:02:46,385 --> 00:02:49,486
In 2024, sales in the United States fall.

53
00:02:49,486 --> 00:02:55,765
Dealer lots fill up with unsold cars, and the company has to warn investors that it

54
00:02:55,765 --> 00:02:57,278
will earn much less.

55
00:02:57,358 --> 00:03:00,237
In September 2024, the company's own U.S.

56
00:03:00,237 --> 00:03:06,135
dealers wrote it an open letter criticizing Tavares over how the business was going.

57
00:03:07,408 --> 00:03:14,531
In Italy, Fiat's birthplace, Stellantis's 2024 production fell to its lowest level

58
00:03:14,531 --> 00:03:18,353
since 1956, according to the FIM-CISL union.

59
00:03:18,808 --> 00:03:22,647
That year's profit ends up at about €5.5 billion.

60
00:03:22,647 --> 00:03:25,939
Seventy percent less than the year before.

61
00:03:26,576 --> 00:03:31,083
And on December 1, 2024, Carlos Tavares leaves the company.

62
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:35,131
Stellantis spoke of "different views" with the board.

63
00:03:35,211 --> 00:03:39,764
According to Reuters, the board was worried that so many cuts were hurting the

64
00:03:39,764 --> 00:03:42,682
quality of the cars and the arrival of new models.

65
00:03:43,968 --> 00:03:47,496
But the real bill for those years hadn't arrived yet.

66
00:03:47,496 --> 00:03:50,891
And when it did, it was the biggest in its history.

67
00:03:51,789 --> 00:03:52,885
Chapter four:

68
00:03:52,885 --> 00:03:53,643
the hole.

69
00:03:54,674 --> 00:03:56,450
February 6, 2026.

70
00:03:56,450 --> 00:04:01,257
Stellantis announces charges of €22.2 billion.

71
00:04:01,257 --> 00:04:08,467
That day, its stock falls as much as 25% on the Milan stock exchange.

72
00:04:08,547 --> 00:04:10,710
Where did such a figure come from?

73
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:14,529
Mostly from electric-car plans that would no longer pay off.

74
00:04:15,175 --> 00:04:18,586
At the end of the month come the results:

75
00:04:18,586 --> 00:04:22,081
a net loss of about €22.3 billion in 2025.

76
00:04:22,081 --> 00:04:26,407
The first annual loss since the company has existed.

77
00:04:26,810 --> 00:04:30,479
And that year, not a single euro of dividends for shareholders.

78
00:04:30,559 --> 00:04:32,355
The official explanation?

79
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:38,030
The new boss, Antonio Filosa, said they had overestimated how fast people would

80
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:39,754
switch to electric cars.

81
00:04:39,834 --> 00:04:45,878
Meanwhile, since April 2025, the United States had been charging 25% tariffs on

82
00:04:45,878 --> 00:04:46,949
imported cars.

83
00:04:46,949 --> 00:04:51,999
Another blow for a company that builds cars across half the world.

84
00:04:52,079 --> 00:04:57,242
And he acknowledged quality problems that he linked to the cuts of the previous era.

85
00:04:57,242 --> 00:04:58,164
In other words:

86
00:04:58,164 --> 00:05:02,406
the recipe behind the record profits also explained part of the hole.

87
00:05:02,486 --> 00:05:04,674
Now, the part almost nobody tells:

88
00:05:04,674 --> 00:05:09,950
while all that was happening in Europe and the United States, in South America the

89
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:11,559
company kept crushing it.

90
00:05:12,209 --> 00:05:13,228
Chapter five:

91
00:05:13,228 --> 00:05:15,501
the South American exception.

92
00:05:15,852 --> 00:05:22,983
In 2025, Stellantis sold almost one in four new cars in South America.

93
00:05:22,983 --> 00:05:24,511
In Brazil, 29%.

94
00:05:24,511 --> 00:05:26,549
In Argentina, 30.5%.

95
00:05:26,629 --> 00:05:29,379
Fiat is the leading brand in the region.

96
00:05:29,379 --> 00:05:34,742
In Brazil, trucks like the Strada, the Toro and the Titano dominate the pickup

97
00:05:34,742 --> 00:05:35,223
market.

98
00:05:35,674 --> 00:05:40,803
The Strada, a small pickup built in Brazil, was the country's best-selling vehicle

99
00:05:40,803 --> 00:05:42,492
for several years in a row.

100
00:05:43,808 --> 00:05:46,665
And in Argentina it has two plants:

101
00:05:46,665 --> 00:05:52,869
Ferreyra, in Córdoba, builds the Fiat Cronos, the Titano and the Ram Dakota.

102
00:05:52,869 --> 00:05:57,848
El Palomar, in Buenos Aires, builds the Peugeot 208 and 2008.

103
00:05:57,928 --> 00:06:04,250
In 2025 alone, the Córdoba plant added about 1,800 workers and became a pickup hub

104
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:05,870
for the whole region.

105
00:06:07,443 --> 00:06:14,006
El Palomar even produced the first electrified cars Argentina built for export:

106
00:06:14,006 --> 00:06:16,665
the hybrid Peugeot 208 and 2008.

107
00:06:17,302 --> 00:06:23,182
According to the company itself, in 2025 it topped one million vehicles sold in

108
00:06:23,182 --> 00:06:24,224
South America.

109
00:06:24,304 --> 00:06:25,934
Why does it work there?

110
00:06:25,934 --> 00:06:26,571
One clue:

111
00:06:26,571 --> 00:06:32,167
in the region it sells affordable, popular cars, exactly what the market wants.

112
00:06:32,167 --> 00:06:34,717
And another clue, even more curious:

113
00:06:34,717 --> 00:06:36,133
who the new boss is.

114
00:06:36,783 --> 00:06:37,843
Chapter six:

115
00:06:37,843 --> 00:06:38,638
what now?

116
00:06:39,303 --> 00:06:45,379
Antonio Filosa, the Italian who took charge in 2025, was head of Stellantis South

117
00:06:45,379 --> 00:06:47,479
America before running Jeep.

118
00:06:48,012 --> 00:06:48,984
In other words:

119
00:06:48,984 --> 00:06:54,300
the man who has to save the giant comes from the one region where it never stopped

120
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,143
making money.

121
00:06:55,833 --> 00:06:57,663
And there are some signs:

122
00:06:57,663 --> 00:07:03,591
in late 2025, Jeep broke a six-year streak of falling sales in the United States.

123
00:07:05,038 --> 00:07:11,963
Also, in 2023 Stellantis bought about 21% of Leapmotor, a Chinese electric-car

124
00:07:11,963 --> 00:07:15,513
maker, to sell its models outside China.

125
00:07:17,222 --> 00:07:19,150
But the road is long.

126
00:07:19,150 --> 00:07:19,976
From U.S.

127
00:07:19,976 --> 00:07:26,495
tariffs alone, the company expects a hit of about €1.6 billion in 2026.

128
00:07:27,733 --> 00:07:29,935
Filosa summed it up like this:

129
00:07:29,935 --> 00:07:34,557
this year, the goal is to close the execution gaps of the past.

130
00:07:34,557 --> 00:07:35,658
In other words:

131
00:07:35,658 --> 00:07:36,758
fix what broke.

132
00:07:36,838 --> 00:07:42,582
So next time you see a Fiat, a Peugeot or a Jeep on the street, remember:

133
00:07:42,582 --> 00:07:47,146
it belongs to a company that lost €22 billion in one year.

134
00:07:47,146 --> 00:07:48,405
Will it survive?

135
00:07:48,405 --> 00:07:49,743
Nobody knows yet.

136
00:07:49,823 --> 00:07:55,204
And yet, in Argentina and Brazil, it still sells almost one in three cars.

137
00:07:55,284 --> 00:07:58,462
Have you ever owned a car from one of its fourteen brands?

138
00:07:58,462 --> 00:07:59,777
Tell me in the comments.

139
00:08:00,741 --> 00:08:05,554
And if you like these stories of companies that rise and fall, subscribe:

140
00:08:05,554 --> 00:08:07,664
every week, a new balance sheet.

